{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/467979-old-clans-still-surviving","id":467979,"title":"Old Clans still Surviving?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-03T16:58:51-07:00","id":467979,"title":"Old Clans still Surviving?","content":"So its established that vampires rarely travel unless circumstances compel them to do so. The 5 clans that exist as they are are only the most abundant or popular in the west. But the book explicitly states that knowledge of foreign Kindred is scarce. It even points this out when explaining about the Burakumin bloodline. And VII is said to have 6 exclusive clans (The Betrayed) in its organization. Not to mention the supposedly extinct Julii and Traditores<br /> <br /> A lot of the old clans such as the Toreador, Bruja, and Giovanni have been reincarnated as bloodlines, but I don't believe all of them were. Is it possible that some of the original clans still exist out there in the world, undiscovered because of their lack of interaction with the western world?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T17:03:50-07:00","id":468000,"title":"","content":"While it's likely there's a lot of clans of vampires that are unknown and undiscovered, given the immortal nature of the Kindred, I think the existence of clans from Vampire the Masquerade would only be likely on the tables of those who decided to homebrew it. Because they never existed in new World of Darkness, so it's not a matter of them 'surviving,' any more than the clans from Blade surviving and making a show.<br /> <br /> Though all of the main clans do have aspects of themselves in Requiem. Not merely as bloodlines, either. That's mainly because Requiem takes advantage of a lot of the stereotypes and iconic vampire fiction that Masquerade did. There's only so much vampire myth to go around, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-03-2015, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T17:51:18-07:00","id":468039,"title":"","content":"My signature has the Salubri ported into NWoD, if you're interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T00:24:50-07:00","id":468171,"title":"","content":"Buy the vampire translation guide, it has write ups for converting the owod clans into clans, bloodlines, or even covenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T16:01:40-07:00","id":468913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/467979-old-clans-still-surviving#post467979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So its established that vampires rarely travel unless circumstances compel them to do so. The 5 clans that exist as they are are only the most abundant or popular in the west. But the book explicitly states that knowledge of foreign Kindred is scarce. It even points this out when explaining about the Burakumin bloodline. And VII is said to have 6 exclusive clans (The Betrayed) in its organization. Not to mention the supposedly extinct Julii and Traditores<br /> <br /> A lot of the old clans such as the Toreador, Bruja, and Giovanni have been reincarnated as bloodlines, but I don't believe all of them were. Is it possible that some of the original clans still exist out there in the world, undiscovered because of their lack of interaction with the western world?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>NWoD clans are more like the theorized OWoD protoclan lineages. You know where they trace second and third gens to figure out which clan came from who.<br /> So Tzim and ventrue may be from a king line. Gangrel and Ravnos from a wild line. <br /> Whereas NWoD bloodlines are specialized versions of the Achetypes represented by NWoD clans and are more like the Clans in OWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T18:35:34-07:00","id":469041,"title":"","content":"Personally, I found each of the 5 clans in nWoD to represent 1 aspect of the vampire mythos. Bestial (Gangrel), Powerful (Ventrue), Charismatic (Daeva), Terrifying (Nosferatu), Graceful (Mekhet). I suppose that the 5 of them together cover all the primary elements of how vampires have been portrayed. Would probably require days worth of research to come up with additional aspects which are missing from the collection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T18:42:04-07:00","id":469044,"title":"","content":"The mekhet seem to originate from some sort of pre-human insectoid. With tentacles. There's no Caine in nWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-04-2015, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T18:58:47-07:00","id":469058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/467979-old-clans-still-surviving?p=469044#post469044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mekhet seem to originate from some sort of pre-human insectoid. With tentacles. There's no Caine in nWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. Unless there is. That's the thing about nWoD, it's a toolbox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T19:03:44-07:00","id":469060,"title":"","content":"That's true, but the toolbox does offer a setting for you and it does seem absent of Caine.<br /> <br /> That said, StSword had some good advice, as the translation guide is very good about adapting the Masquerade clans over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T19:41:37-07:00","id":469091,"title":"","content":"They appear to have shied away from Cain stories simply because that's old world of darkness. No reason your vampires can't believe in Cain, or at least some of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T20:06:40-07:00","id":469099,"title":"","content":"I, personally, use a modified VtM for my VtR games, dropping Generation for Blood Potency and a Merit, while using all the clans. This is obviously not 'canon' but you can successfully merge them by spinning a few concepts (Strix, Revenants) if you wish to have them in your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T05:43:42-07:00","id":469295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/467979-old-clans-still-surviving?p=469044#post469044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mekhet seem to originate from some sort of pre-human insectoid. With tentacles. There's no Caine in nWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I wasn't talking about Caine, though, I was curious if it was possible for other clans (newly interpreted for Requiem) to still exist throughout the world, and not be recognized. Gangrel, Nosferatu and Ventrue still exist, but they're not from Caine... as far as we can tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T07:25:57-07:00","id":469327,"title":"","content":"I think the &quot;still&quot; is throwing people off, because in Requiem those other clans never existed (unless the ST wants to deviate from the default setting assumptions). But yes, it's possible to translate Masquerade Clans to Requiem. Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke#post5268\">Yossarian's 13 licks thread</a> to see some examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T07:57:53-07:00","id":469339,"title":"","content":"Oh, sorry about that. I meant still surviving from Masquerade into Requiem. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T08:06:34-07:00","id":469343,"title":"","content":"One cannot survive from Masquerade into Requiem because the settings are completely separate. One can port clans/concepts/anything from one to the other, but that's not the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T08:25:08-07:00","id":469361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/467979-old-clans-still-surviving?p=469339#post469339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, sorry about that. I meant still surviving from Masquerade into Requiem. :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be explicit:<br /> <br /> In Vampire: The Masquerade, all 13 clans descend from Caine. In the 1400s, groups called the Camarilla and Sabbat formed, and survive to the present day.<br /> <br /> In Vampire: The Requiem, there are somewhere around seven clans, each with a separate origin (possibly multiple separate origins). A group called the Camarilla was formed in the BCE era, but collapsed with the fall of Rome in 476 CE.<br /> <br /> The two settings both have vampires and both have clans with similar names, but they both take place in different universes entirely. Masquerade is not the past of Requiem, and Requiem is not the future of Masquerade.<br /> <br /> With the Translation Guide you can use elements of Masquerade in Requiem, or Requiem in Masquerade, but by default they're two completely separate things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T08:26:29-07:00","id":469363,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure Nyrufa means &quot;surviving&quot; from an out-of-character perspective, like a passage in a book that survives the editing process from one draft to another, or like a mechanic in an RPG that survives an edition change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T09:30:40-07:00","id":469394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/467979-old-clans-still-surviving?p=469060#post469060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true, but the toolbox does offer a setting for you and it does seem absent of Caine.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not absent of Caine. In Requiem for Rome there was an heretic branch of the Lancea et Sanctum who believed Caine was the first vampire, and has survived in current days as a Hunter conspiracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T10:54:22-07:00","id":469410,"title":"","content":"I believe that was more in reference to the actual <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cainites\" target=\"_blank\">Cainite</a> heresy, rather than the depiction of Caine from Vampire the Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T12:58:39-07:00","id":469557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/467979-old-clans-still-surviving?p=469394#post469394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not absent of Caine. In Requiem for Rome there was an heretic branch of the Lancea et Sanctum who believed Caine was the first vampire, and has survived in current days as a Hunter conspiracy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> First edition Requiem (Which I still go by, since I haven't bought B&amp;S) suggests that the vampires don't actually know their origins, and the fact Torpor screws with their minds doesn't help either. There actually could be Caine, and they just don't remember him. From what I've heard around the forums and see in Gentleman Gamer's videos, B&amp;S gave a more concrete explanation for where they originated from.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah, I know they're separate universes, and Charlaquin was right. I meant from one literature to the next, not story-wise carry over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T13:03:03-07:00","id":469561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/467979-old-clans-still-surviving?p=469557#post469557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I've heard around the forums and see in Gentleman Gamer's videos, B&amp;S gave a more concrete explanation for where they originated from.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really, unless you mean they included 3 or 4 different possible origins per Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T13:07:06-07:00","id":469566,"title":"","content":"First edition did have a lot of theories, probably most well described in the clan books, which is where the revelation of mekhet's pre-human ancestry comes from. While Blood and Smoke offers some origins, they're no more or less valid than those from first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T13:09:13-07:00","id":469567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/467979-old-clans-still-surviving?p=469561#post469561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not really, unless you mean they included 3 or 4 different possible origins per Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah, well if that's the case, he provides one possible origin for each, anyways.<br /> <br /> Mekhet being from Egypt, Gangrel being descended from slaves of Rome, est.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hJRyu_e0rqI&amp;list=PL2DxDtkXbv2jQtfJJm7I1mAdhCWp7ApwA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hJRyu_e0rqI&amp;list=PL2DxDtkXbv2jQtfJJm7I1mAdhCWp7ApwA\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hJRyu_e0rqI&amp;list=PL2DxDtkXbv2jQtfJJm7I1mAdhCWp7ApwA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hJRyu_e0rqI&amp;list=PL2DxDtkXbv2jQtfJJm7I1mAdhCWp7ApwA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T13:12:46-07:00","id":469570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/467979-old-clans-still-surviving?p=469557#post469557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First edition Requiem (Which I still go by, since I haven't bought B&amp;S) suggests that the vampires don't actually know their origins, and the fact Torpor screws with their minds doesn't help either. There actually could be Caine, and they just don't remember him. From what I've heard around the forums and see in Gentleman Gamer's videos, B&amp;S gave a more concrete explanation for where they originated from.</div> </div> </div> </div>As of 2nd edition, memory loss during torpor does happen, but it is a relatively uncommon occurrence, so Kindred history is far more reliable. That said, the origins of vampires is still a matter of much speculation. I say origins, because it is all but certain that they did not all come from a single progenitor. Instead, the Clans are most likely all different kinds of undead creatures, which have grown more similar over time through convergent evolution. In fact, there are multiple origin myths even within the same clan. So short of a massive setting overhaul, Cain as the progenitor of all vampires is right out. That doesn't preclude the possibility of Cain existing and being an ancient, powerful vampire, perhaps even the founder of one or more vampiric lineages. But that would be custom setting material for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T13:22:19-07:00","id":469573,"title":"","content":"The whole God thing is way fuzzier in new WoD, for one thing. (There's about three or so distinct entities who <i>might </i>be the guy in the books alone) So Caine's origins themselves probably need an overhaul to fit right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T19:09:45-07:00","id":469747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/467979-old-clans-still-surviving?p=469557#post469557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> First edition Requiem (Which I still go by, since I haven't bought B&amp;S) suggests that the vampires don't actually know their origins, and the fact Torpor screws with their minds doesn't help either. There actually could be Caine, and they just don't remember him. From what I've heard around the forums and see in Gentleman Gamer's videos, B&amp;S gave a more concrete explanation for where they originated from.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah, I know they're separate universes, and Charlaquin was right. I meant from one literature to the next, not story-wise carry over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look there is the Chroniclers Guide and Danse Macabre which offer intriguing origins.<br /> Blood and Smoke offer even more options. <br /> Don't forget Spontaneous embraces.<br /> Mithra, the serpent from Eden, Roman Royalty, that first one of each clan was self embraced because of a certain fear, you can on and on.<br /> It is a feature not a bug.<br /> But if you want roll Cain into the original vamp, you can. But I prefer Gilgamesh myself.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But I would read the clan books and see what they say before you decide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T02:17:54-07:00","id":469985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/467979-old-clans-still-surviving?p=469573#post469573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole God thing is way fuzzier in new WoD, for one thing. (There's about three or so distinct entities who <i>might </i>be the guy in the books alone) So Caine's origins themselves probably need an overhaul to fit right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cain was/is/served/controls a/the strix.<br /> Done","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T14:09:15-07:00","id":473305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/467979-old-clans-still-surviving#post467979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So its established that vampires rarely travel unless circumstances compel them to do so. The 5 clans that exist as they are are only the most abundant or popular in the west. But the book explicitly states that knowledge of foreign Kindred is scarce. It even points this out when explaining about the Burakumin bloodline. And VII is said to have 6 exclusive clans (The Betrayed) in its organization. Not to mention the supposedly extinct Julii and Traditores<br /> <br /> A lot of the old clans such as the Toreador, Bruja, and Giovanni have been reincarnated as bloodlines, but I don't believe all of them were. Is it possible that some of the original clans still exist out there in the world, undiscovered because of their lack of interaction with the western world?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes if you want them. Personally I see Banu Haqim as a small group or Bloodline of Mekhet. Your milage may vary.<br /> Are the Tzim Lordly Nos or or Scarey Lords?<br /> NWoD is designed so that you can put whatever spin you want on it.<br /> That is a feature not a bug!<br /> <br /> WARNING: Those of us who do port something old over each have our own way of doing it.<br /> But there is no<i> right way. </i>Just opinion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T04:10:49-07:00","id":480054,"title":"","content":"As others have covered pretty well already, the 5 clans in Requiem cover sort of different conceptual ground than in Masquerade, something between root/proto-clans or even variant brands/species of bloodthirsty undead as &quot;Cainite&quot;, &quot;Kuei-jin&quot; or &quot;Laibon&quot; (yeah, i'm fudging it up) in oWoD, so to speak.<br /> <br /> Any of the commented origins may be valid and maybe even several at the same time - while the Mekhet clanbook speaks of a origin in egypt as some-sort of mummy-like undead, it also throws at us a blood sympathy-induced flashback of a lovecraftian horror attacking cavemen (if not hominids) <b>and</b> to further monkeywrench things, a bloodline that, while in the Mekhet book, references a viking-era iceland origin as &quot;clan Grettir&quot; - what indirectly also strikes home on the subject &quot;are the Julii a true separate clan or just independently spawned/variant Ventrue, or vice-versa?&quot;, not to mention some bloodlines in other boks that claim to be the source of their respective clans instead of the opposite as would be expected, like the Rakshasa (in Bloodlines: the Hidden) and Vedma (in the OD book).<br /> <br /> So, yeah, there's room for different clans in different areas of the world. Blood &amp; Smoke itself has one sample (with hooks on the non-kindred from Wicked Dead to boot) 6th clan, in a most unlikely place in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-05-2015, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}